config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_AIRPURIFIER
	bool "Domoticz plugin: Xiaomi air purifiers"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_MIIO
	default n
	help
		control of the Xiaomi / Mi air purifiers that answer the miIO
		protocol (AirPurifier 2 and the related models) over the LAN

		It is a Python plugin of Domoticz: the package installs it into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/domoticz-AirPurifier, the directory Domoticz is
		started with (-approot of the domoticz package), and it needs no
		change of the Domoticz build.

		The plugin needs python-miio (installed as a dependency of this
		package) in addition to the standard library. python-miio speaks
		to the device directly on the LAN, so no Xiaomi account is used:
		the address of the purifier and its token are the settings of the
		plugin (the token is read out of the Xiaomi Home app or of a
		miiocli based tool once).

		Setup: Setup -> Hardware -> AirPurifier, enter the address of the
		purifier in Address and its token in Mode1.

		The upstream repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a
		pinned commit of the default branch. Upstream ships no license
		file: the README is installed with the plugin.
